From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 16:03:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 11/12] LvglDisplayEngineDxe: Draw a dynamic wallpaper, blur
 the bars over it

The desktop was a flat #121212. Draw a wallpaper instead, like a dynamic
desktop: a vertical sky gradient across the screen and three soft orbs
of color over it, circles filled with a radial gradient that fades to
transparent at the edge, in a palette that follows the hour of the RTC
(night, dawn, day, dusk, evening). The clock timer of the menu bar
switches the palette when the hour moves into another band; nothing is
animated, and the orbs are only redrawn where the screen is invalidated.
The radial gradients need LV_USE_DRAW_SW_COMPLEX_GRADIENTS, enabled in
lv_conf.h; THEME_WALLPAPER 0 keeps the flat desktop.

With a wallpaper to show through, the menu bar and the dock become
translucent, with the backdrop blurred behind them and a faint light
rim, as on macOS. The window gets a wider, softer shadow and a title bar
shaded from top to bottom; the tiles of the front page and the key caps
of the dock are lit from the top; the colored squares of the menu
symbols darken towards the bottom, like app icons.

Co-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
